WEBVTT

00:11.110 --> 00:13.740
I've decided to participate in that project.

00:14.220 --> 00:17.320
It looks like I won't be able to come back here for a while.

00:36.030 --> 00:39.950
What you were saying might actually become reality in the other place.

00:45.950 --> 00:49.060
Well then, I'll be going...

00:49.060 --> 00:49.880
Yuko.

00:51.960 --> 00:54.400
Renji-kun, it's morning.

00:54.700 --> 00:56.660
Renji-kun.

00:58.340 --> 00:59.700
Good morning...

01:00.770 --> 01:02.700
Merry Christmas...

01:03.970 --> 01:05.370
Renji-kun.

01:05.370 --> 01:08.000
M-Merry Christmas...

01:08.100 --> 01:09.320
Chihiro.

01:15.260 --> 01:18.290
I went to wake up Renji-kun, Auntie.

01:18.290 --> 01:19.640
Thanks.

01:21.720 --> 01:23.140
I guess it tastes okay.

01:23.390 --> 01:25.390
What do you think, Chihiro-chan?

01:27.210 --> 01:28.650
It's very good!

01:30.230 --> 01:32.190
The weather is nice today.

01:32.630 --> 01:34.990
It looks like perfect weather for Christmas.

01:39.320 --> 01:39.950
All right.

01:39.950 --> 01:41.450
I'm done.

01:45.090 --> 01:47.650
Oh, morning, Miyako.

01:47.650 --> 01:52.380
You're supposed to say "Merry Christmas", Hiro-kun.

01:53.590 --> 01:57.010
There's no Christmas or Bon or New Year's Day for a mangaka.

01:53.590 --> 01:57.010
Bon is a Japanese Buddhist festival to honor the deceased spirits of one's ancestors.

01:57.010 --> 02:00.760
There you go again, talking like your life is so terribly unpleasant.

02:00.760 --> 02:03.760
There's no New Year's Day, but there is New Year's progress.

02:03.760 --> 02:06.770
Jeez, your words don't contain any dreams.

02:07.140 --> 02:09.580
Just come in. Aren't you cold?

02:09.580 --> 02:10.420
Yeah!

02:13.790 --> 02:16.030
It sure is snowing a lot this year.

02:16.030 --> 02:18.900
Yeah, it'll be a white Christmas!

02:18.900 --> 02:22.030
This school I'm so used to seeing seems like a completely different world.

02:22.130 --> 02:25.040
Yeah! It's all white and really beautiful.

02:25.130 --> 02:28.290
Hey, quit chattering and help out!

02:28.560 --> 02:31.910
If we don't hurry, we won't make it to the screening on time.

02:31.910 --> 02:33.040
Roger!

02:33.140 --> 02:35.300
Well then, I'll be going.

02:35.930 --> 02:38.170
Kyousuke, I'll help out too.

02:38.170 --> 02:39.680
No, you can relax.

02:39.770 --> 02:42.730
Nah, if I stay still, I'll get cold!

02:42.730 --> 02:45.430
Okay. Well, I'll be counting on you, Kei-chan.

02:45.430 --> 02:46.520
Production Screening
Experimental Film Club

02:46.520 --> 02:48.140
Those two really piss me off!

02:56.340 --> 02:58.130
I can't decide...

02:58.130 --> 03:01.030
This one's good, but I want to wear this one, too.

03:01.030 --> 03:04.240
I also want to wear this other one that I just wore for the first time recently!

03:05.090 --> 03:07.040
Which one do you think is better, Shuichi?

03:11.760 --> 03:12.620
Yo.

03:12.850 --> 03:13.880
Nagi.

03:13.880 --> 03:15.160
It's been a while.

03:15.160 --> 03:16.000
When did you get here?

03:16.190 --> 03:17.980
I arrived just a little while ago.

03:17.980 --> 03:20.010
I was in Japan until yesterday.

03:20.480 --> 03:22.910
Like always, you're good at drawing scenery.

03:22.910 --> 03:25.760
Still, I could never get the hang of drawing people.

03:25.760 --> 03:27.700
Your foundation wasn't good, yeah.

03:27.700 --> 03:29.350
But it was sufficient as a work of art.

03:29.350 --> 03:31.580
If the foundation is bad, then won't everything else be bad too?

03:31.580 --> 03:33.900
That's only if you're talking about technique.

03:33.900 --> 03:36.900
If you put your soul in it, then the result will outshine the technique.

03:37.090 --> 03:39.530
You're going to lecture me about art <i>now?</i>

03:40.360 --> 03:42.860
I'm your senior when it comes to art, you know.

03:42.860 --> 03:46.740
As long as you don't get expelled, you're still my student.

03:47.810 --> 03:49.910
Some senior, eh?

03:49.910 --> 03:51.290
Is Kuze doing all right?

03:51.290 --> 03:54.900
Yeah. He can't overwork himself, but he's living normally.

03:54.900 --> 03:55.960
And also...

03:58.460 --> 03:59.950
I see.

03:59.950 --> 04:00.960
You're right.

04:00.960 --> 04:03.790
Have you decided where to stay yet?

04:03.790 --> 04:07.050
Nah. Let me stay at your place again.

04:07.050 --> 04:07.930
No.

04:07.930 --> 04:08.850
Why not?

04:09.220 --> 04:11.840
I've finished the tough part of the job here.

04:11.840 --> 04:13.480
I'm going back to Japan soon.

04:13.940 --> 04:16.760
I've decided to leave Chihiro in Renji's care as well.

04:16.760 --> 04:17.870
I see.

04:17.870 --> 04:20.080
Go stay at Kuze's place or something.

04:20.080 --> 04:21.490
He'll be delighted to have visitors.

04:22.590 --> 04:24.570
He's really changed, hasn't he?

04:24.880 --> 04:26.660
People normally would.

04:28.370 --> 04:29.230
Yu.

04:29.230 --> 04:30.230
What is it?

04:30.230 --> 04:34.330
Do you... still have feelings for her?

04:35.540 --> 04:36.740
Who knows?

04:36.740 --> 04:38.110
I've forgotten already.

04:38.110 --> 04:41.880
It feels odd saying this to you <i>now, but...</i>

04:42.800 --> 04:43.630
What is it?

05:19.680 --> 05:34.740
Alone on the street corner when it's beginning to grow dark.

05:35.680 --> 05:50.860
The melody that flutters before the shining stars and the sunset

05:55.660 --> 06:11.630
is love that whispers to the light of the moon.

05:59.150 --> 06:00.960
Don't you have to rest?

06:00.960 --> 06:02.340
You're tired, aren't you?

06:02.340 --> 06:04.710
It's just moderate exercise.

06:05.150 --> 06:08.300
If I could extend my lifespan by a minute or even a second,

06:08.300 --> 06:09.880
I'd believe what anyone says,

06:09.880 --> 06:12.100
whether it's a sardine's head or a doctor.

06:11.630 --> 06:26.710
A melody that stays in the wind. I meet my true love.

06:12.310 --> 06:14.620
A doctor and a sardine are in the same category?

06:14.620 --> 06:17.890
If they give me results, then they're all the same.

06:18.980 --> 06:23.130
To think that I could celebrate another Christmas like this...

06:23.130 --> 06:23.900
Are you dissatisfied?

06:24.780 --> 06:28.260
This world is worse than you imagine,

06:28.260 --> 06:30.660
but also better than you think.

06:31.520 --> 06:34.590
It looks like you'll be fine, even without me.

06:34.590 --> 06:36.640
She'll be an adult soon.

06:36.640 --> 06:37.330
Yeah.

06:37.660 --> 06:40.670
She'll probably be stunningly beautiful in a year.

06:41.420 --> 06:42.720
Yeah.

06:42.720 --> 06:44.950
And a year after that, even more so.

06:44.950 --> 06:45.670
Yeah.

06:45.980 --> 06:49.880
I wonder how long I can watch her.

06:52.590 --> 06:54.930
If you want to keep watching, then live a long life.

06:55.960 --> 06:57.060
I will.

06:57.210 --> 06:59.050
Even if I have to cling to it.

06:59.050 --> 07:02.810
It really looks like my job here is done.

07:03.020 --> 07:04.690
We won't be seeing each other for a while.

07:04.880 --> 07:06.080
You're leaving?

07:06.080 --> 07:08.030
I'm going back to the real Otowa.

07:08.030 --> 07:12.020
It's earlier than I'd planned, but I want to be there for the Christmas season.

07:12.020 --> 07:13.830
Did something happen?

07:13.830 --> 07:15.090
I don't know.

07:15.090 --> 07:16.680
That's why I have to go and see.

07:16.680 --> 07:18.260
It's cold over there, you know.

07:18.260 --> 07:20.410
Make sure you take warm clothing.

07:21.160 --> 07:22.780
This is a parting gift.

07:22.780 --> 07:24.170
This is...

07:24.290 --> 07:26.380
The place where everything begins

07:26.620 --> 07:28.510
It's a charm that brings forth miracles.

07:28.700 --> 07:32.940
You may not believe it, but it brought me results.

07:32.940 --> 07:34.760
Danke, Kuze.

07:35.110 --> 07:37.390
Gute Reise, Himura.

07:41.640 --> 07:45.720
It feels odd saying this to you <i>now, but...</i>

07:45.720 --> 07:46.930
What is it?

07:46.930 --> 07:50.820
When I returned to Japan, my little brother said something weird.

07:50.820 --> 07:51.820
Hiro did?

07:51.820 --> 07:55.200
Yeah. He said that he met "her" at the church.

07:56.280 --> 07:57.950
Who's this "her"?

07:58.330 --> 07:59.410
Yuko

07:59.410 --> 08:00.410
What?

08:00.410 --> 08:04.420
Hiro said that he met Amamiya Yuko.

08:45.040 --> 08:48.540
How far will the wings carry you

08:45.040 --> 08:48.540
Find me, hidden in your feelings

09:47.640 --> 09:49.020
It's unfortunate,

09:49.530 --> 09:51.770
but Mass is already over.

09:52.820 --> 09:55.030
I'm not a believer.

09:55.450 --> 09:57.560
There's someone I need to see.

09:57.560 --> 09:58.580
What about you?

09:58.580 --> 10:02.990
I'm just waiting for someone.

10:04.040 --> 10:07.440
I made you wait for quite a long time, didn't I?

10:07.440 --> 10:11.130
I've only been waiting for a little while.

10:11.130 --> 10:13.620
Sorry about that, Yuko.

10:13.800 --> 10:16.540
It's been a while, Yu-kun.

10:16.540 --> 10:19.300
I'm surprised you remembered.

10:19.630 --> 10:23.550
I didn't forget for an instant.

10:23.860 --> 10:27.560
This is the Christmas present I couldn't give you.

10:29.060 --> 10:30.420
Thank you.

10:30.420 --> 10:33.900
Even though there's nothing I can give in return...

10:33.900 --> 10:38.270
No, I received that a long time ago.

10:39.530 --> 10:41.030
That's...

10:41.590 --> 10:43.160
Merry Christmas.

10:43.660 --> 10:45.910
Merry Christmas.

10:46.980 --> 10:49.180
It's quiet tonight.

10:49.180 --> 10:53.230
Yeah. It's as if we're the only two in this world.

10:53.230 --> 10:55.350
A world with only you, Yu-kun...

10:55.350 --> 10:57.220
Every day would be fun.

10:57.220 --> 10:58.270
Yeah.

10:58.270 --> 11:02.590
But knowing you, you'd probably take advantage of the lack of observers

11:02.590 --> 11:04.620
and be mean to me.

11:04.620 --> 11:06.430
You're quite rude sometimes.

11:07.530 --> 11:12.690
But in all honesty, I don't want anyone to interfere with this moment.

11:12.850 --> 11:14.170
Me neither,

11:14.170 --> 11:17.400
since I was finally able to fulfill my promise to you.

11:17.620 --> 11:19.780
It's been a long time, hasn't it?

11:19.780 --> 11:22.980
Miki's probably grown up now, hasn't she?

11:22.980 --> 11:26.530
She's probably enjoying a summer Christmas with Kuze right now.

11:26.530 --> 11:28.620
A summer Christmas?

11:28.620 --> 11:30.850
You were talking about it, weren't you?

11:30.850 --> 11:33.270
Do you want to go to Australia?

11:33.270 --> 11:35.770
No, it's fine.

11:35.770 --> 11:38.800
As long as Miki is enjoying a summer Christmas.

11:38.800 --> 11:39.960
I see.

11:40.700 --> 11:45.010
But to think that we'd reunite after such a long time...

11:45.290 --> 11:53.940
The collective wishes of all the people we've met and touched allowed us to meet again.

11:53.940 --> 11:55.770
It feels that way.

11:55.770 --> 12:00.030
That's a romantic way to think of it. It's not like you.

12:00.030 --> 12:02.370
Miracles don't exist in the world.

12:02.370 --> 12:04.530
The only things that exist are
coincidences and inevitabilities,

12:04.530 --> 12:07.150
and the actions people take.

12:07.320 --> 12:10.110
I've always believed that.

12:10.110 --> 12:11.660
That's fine.

12:11.850 --> 12:16.290
Miracles don't happen to people who just wish for them.

12:16.700 --> 12:22.470
A helping hand is only extended to people
who are trying to cause a miracle themselves.

12:29.620 --> 12:33.390
There was something I had to do.

12:33.390 --> 12:35.560
Something you had to do?

12:35.840 --> 12:41.480
It was my duty to always be kind to as many people as possible,

12:41.480 --> 12:45.890
and to give everything for the benefit of others.

12:45.890 --> 12:48.320
He told me to do it.

12:48.320 --> 12:49.530
Who?

12:49.530 --> 12:50.580
Who knows?

12:50.780 --> 12:53.870
Maybe it was God.

12:53.870 --> 12:55.200
God?

12:55.200 --> 12:59.450
You told me in the past that there is no God, right?

12:59.450 --> 13:00.490
Yeah.

13:00.490 --> 13:02.340
Do you still believe that?

13:03.670 --> 13:08.640
I'll continue living by believing in myself and in the people around me.

13:09.760 --> 13:12.770
Since I'm only able to live the way I am now.

13:12.770 --> 13:15.100
That's just like you.

13:15.400 --> 13:17.480
Yuko, do you want to go?

13:17.480 --> 13:18.480
Huh?

13:21.940 --> 13:25.440
Our starting place.

13:21.940 --> 13:23.070
Our

13:25.640 --> 13:26.900
Yes!

13:35.870 --> 13:38.040
I've always wanted to do this.

13:38.670 --> 13:39.710
Yeah.

13:39.710 --> 13:42.660
My dream also came true.

13:42.660 --> 13:47.300
Yuko, there's something I couldn't say to you back then.

13:47.300 --> 13:49.050
I...

13:49.340 --> 13:51.300
love you.

13:51.500 --> 13:53.220
Yu-kun...

13:53.370 --> 13:55.200
I love you, Yuko.

13:55.200 --> 13:57.980
I'm sorry I couldn't say it for so long.

13:57.980 --> 13:59.510
You're wrong there.

13:59.510 --> 14:00.480
Huh?

14:00.480 --> 14:02.730
You mean, "I loved you", right?

14:02.890 --> 14:04.310
Yuko...

14:04.310 --> 14:06.710
I was happy.

14:06.710 --> 14:09.860
I'm so glad I was able to meet you.

14:10.670 --> 14:12.780
Thank you for loving me.

14:12.780 --> 14:15.370
Thank you for all the happiness you gave me.

14:15.370 --> 14:18.210
Those are words that should be coming out of <i>my mouth.</i>

14:18.210 --> 14:22.080
It looks like I've done everything I can for this town.

14:22.770 --> 14:24.840
Oh, so you're going to leave now.

14:25.280 --> 14:26.600
I'm sorry.

14:26.600 --> 14:31.590
Since you're someone who can make decisions for yourself, please continue to move forward.

14:31.590 --> 14:32.320
Yeah.

14:32.320 --> 14:34.380
I'll be sure to move forward.

14:34.380 --> 14:36.770
I'm truly... sorry.

14:36.770 --> 14:38.860
You have nothing to apologize for.

14:38.860 --> 14:40.020
I'm fine now.

14:47.790 --> 14:48.900
Yu-kun...

14:49.090 --> 14:52.570
At the moment, I'm neither lonely nor in pain.

14:52.780 --> 14:55.450
I can go anywhere on my own.

14:58.480 --> 14:59.870
It's all right.

14:59.870 --> 15:01.620
Don't worry about me.

15:02.860 --> 15:05.880
Just as I'd expect of Yu-kun.

15:06.070 --> 15:10.740
Please share the happiness you gave me with other people, too.

15:10.740 --> 15:17.570
If you do that, then those wishes and that happiness might return to us someday.

15:17.570 --> 15:19.960
Yeah, they probably will.

15:19.960 --> 15:23.900
Both the wishes and that happiness will reach to infinite distances.

15:29.190 --> 15:31.200
Today was fun.

15:31.200 --> 15:33.320
It's as if I'm dreaming.

15:33.650 --> 15:35.320
It's not a dream.

15:35.530 --> 15:40.650
Memories are precious, but please
continue looking towards the future.

15:40.650 --> 15:41.330
Yeah.

15:41.580 --> 15:44.590
And please don't look back anymore.

15:44.590 --> 15:48.990
Please... without turning back... be happy.

15:48.990 --> 15:52.150
That's all I wish for.

15:52.150 --> 15:53.090
Yeah.

15:53.300 --> 15:56.220
Good bye, Yu-kun...

15:56.840 --> 16:01.970
I've always... loved you too.

16:34.170 --> 16:36.260
She... really...

16:39.090 --> 16:43.100
I guess even an angel... wants some time to rest.

16:51.500 --> 16:53.940
Himura-san, who are you exactly?

16:54.210 --> 16:55.670
I'm an architect.

16:55.670 --> 17:01.550
My job right now is to make sure that the people here can live happily.

17:01.550 --> 17:03.950
It looks exactly the same as the Otowa in Japan.

17:04.090 --> 17:07.720
It's as if you're dreaming, isn't it?

17:07.720 --> 17:11.860
Everything begins from a dream.

17:11.860 --> 17:13.250
"I want to fly the skies."

17:13.250 --> 17:14.870
"I want to see the depths of the sea."

17:14.870 --> 17:16.260
"I want to go into space."

17:16.260 --> 17:18.840
"I want to reach that distant star."

17:19.500 --> 17:24.520
To keep on dreaming... that's the first step in making a dream come true.

17:24.830 --> 17:27.270
I wanted to make a beautiful city.

17:27.690 --> 17:32.480
A city where everyone is kind, and no one will be left alone.

17:32.480 --> 17:35.150
A bright city that's connected to the future.

17:35.300 --> 17:37.330
That's a wonderful dream.

17:37.330 --> 17:40.540
And that became reality in two forms.

17:40.540 --> 17:43.020
Two cities by the name of Otowa exist:

17:43.020 --> 17:46.980
the real city built upon burned-down bricks,

17:46.980 --> 17:51.500
and the fraudulent city, which has carried the city's image to peaceful, beautiful lands.

17:51.660 --> 17:53.880
It isn't fraudulent.

17:54.840 --> 17:55.840
All of it...

17:55.840 --> 17:56.840
All of it...

17:57.130 --> 17:58.740
All of it...

17:58.740 --> 18:00.180
is real.

18:00.180 --> 18:02.850
The city, and the people living in it.

18:03.090 --> 18:08.100
Because a lie that is told for the good of others isn't a lie at all.

18:17.450 --> 18:19.890
The people that we love are living here,

18:19.890 --> 18:24.350
and our thoughts for the people that we love built this city.

18:24.350 --> 18:28.330
This city and the other city are filled with true happiness.

18:28.520 --> 18:30.020
I see.

18:30.020 --> 18:31.080
You're right.

18:32.790 --> 18:34.030
I'm sorry!

18:34.030 --> 18:35.730
It's a bad habit of mine.

18:35.730 --> 18:37.380
You don't have to hold hands anymore?

18:37.380 --> 18:40.380
It's fine. I'm not a child, you know!

18:40.710 --> 18:42.140
Are you sure it's okay?

18:43.240 --> 18:46.390
Himura-san, you're like a father.

18:47.360 --> 18:49.490
That's not bad either.

18:49.490 --> 18:52.070
You're not having nightmares anymore?

18:52.070 --> 18:54.820
No, not anymore.

18:56.820 --> 18:59.790
I never actually asked you for your name.

18:59.790 --> 19:01.410
It's Hayama Mizuki.

19:03.070 --> 19:07.110
But when I was little... people called me Miki.

19:07.110 --> 19:09.000
You write "future", and read it as "Miki".

19:09.370 --> 19:10.620
I see.

19:13.810 --> 19:15.250
That's a good name.

19:16.750 --> 19:23.140
towa ni hitotsu no negai kanaete

19:16.750 --> 19:23.140
Love, I've got to feel it
If you put your trust in me

19:23.140 --> 19:31.510
itsuka mirai wo mune ni dakishimete

19:23.140 --> 19:31.510
I know what my life would be
Oh, you are all I ever need

19:31.510 --> 19:43.410
yami no mukou ni kieru anata no koe

19:31.510 --> 19:43.410
I try to hear what you say
So I pray, but you're fading away

19:44.410 --> 19:53.960
ude nobashita kedo todokanai

19:44.410 --> 19:53.960
Don't go and break my fragile heart
We won't fall apart

19:53.960 --> 20:01.880
kage wo oikake

19:53.960 --> 20:01.880
'Cause you're my only star

20:03.930 --> 20:11.140
hashiridasu sekai ga kokoro kizutsuketemo

20:03.930 --> 20:11.140
I wonder why my tears come at night
Calling you, so like a little child

20:11.140 --> 20:17.770
nigiru sono te wo hanasanaide ite

20:11.140 --> 20:17.770
All the things you have in mind
I wish I could see your insides

20:17.770 --> 20:24.400
hateshinaku sora e narihibike kono merodii

20:17.770 --> 20:24.400
My love, you've got to feel it
And if we put our trust in you and me

20:24.400 --> 20:35.960
afureru namida wo wasure wa shinai wa

20:24.400 --> 20:35.960
You know what our lives would be
Oh, you are the one, I believe

20:47.150 --> 20:49.380
The wind blows through the streets.

20:49.380 --> 20:53.640
The wind is cold, and there are times when we want to stop.

20:53.640 --> 20:57.290
At times like that, I want you to move forward, even if it's just at a slow pace.

20:57.290 --> 21:00.340
Because someday, you'll be able to get there.

21:00.340 --> 21:02.790
Even if something sad happens, it's all right.

21:02.790 --> 21:05.740
If you extend your hand, someone will be there.

21:05.740 --> 21:08.470
And you'll be able to share the warmth with them.

21:08.470 --> 21:10.580
Even if it's tough to journey on your own,

21:10.580 --> 21:12.320
if you don't let go of the hand you hold,

21:12.320 --> 21:13.950
you'll surely be able to pull through.

21:13.950 --> 21:16.250
So, please don't give up.

21:16.250 --> 21:20.430
Happiness awaits at the end of the long, long road.

21:20.430 --> 21:22.280
That happiness builds up,

21:22.280 --> 21:24.310
and grows into something even larger.

21:24.310 --> 21:27.260
And someday, I want you to realize

21:27.260 --> 21:29.490
that there were numerous shards of happiness

21:29.490 --> 21:31.820
on the road you just walked.

21:31.820 --> 21:33.190
Please don't forget

21:33.190 --> 21:35.270
that you are not alone.

21:35.270 --> 21:37.100
Engraving your footsteps,

21:37.100 --> 21:38.160
crossing the seasons,

21:38.160 --> 21:39.930
and looking up at the sky.

21:39.930 --> 21:43.070
Even if you don't have wings,
you'll definitely be able to get there.

21:43.070 --> 21:44.930
To the place that you once dreamed of.

21:44.930 --> 21:47.830
To the tomorrow that gleams with light-

21:52.480 --> 22:05.170
mune ni kakushita omoi wa setsunakute

21:52.480 --> 22:05.170
The feelings that I hid inside my chest were painful.

22:06.310 --> 22:18.350
obieta kokoro sukoshi dake yuraideita

22:06.310 --> 22:18.350
My frightened heart wavered just a little.

22:20.350 --> 22:27.190
wasurenai wa ano hi no koto

22:20.350 --> 22:27.190
I'll never forget about that day.

22:27.190 --> 22:40.780
te to te tsunagu futari kanashimi koete yuku

22:27.190 --> 22:40.780
We held hands to overcome the sadness.

22:41.370 --> 22:47.890
doko made mo doko made mo hashire

22:41.370 --> 22:47.890
Run forever, to wherever.

22:47.890 --> 22:54.890
ude no naka ai dakishimete hashire

22:47.890 --> 22:54.890
Run while embracing love in your arms.

22:54.890 --> 23:02.760
tsubasa nante nakute kamawanai

22:54.890 --> 23:02.760
It's all right if you don't have wings.

23:02.760 --> 23:09.590
dakara todokote futari e

23:02.760 --> 23:09.590
So please, deliver it to them...

23:09.590 --> 23:16.760
towa ni kawaranu ano sora

23:09.590 --> 23:16.760
the sky that will never change.
